-    - name: Renaming ID tag
-      description: |
-        The ID tag must exactly match the Flatpak ID. If it has to be renamed completely, the application needs to be resubmitted.
-        The ID tag in the MetaInfo file is supposed to be a constant and unique identifier of an application and should not be renamed unless absolutely necessary.
-        If a rename is necessary, please add the old ID tag as a provides tag and a replaces tag in the MetaInfo file.
-        rename-appdata-file in the Flatpak manifest can automatically update the ID tag in the MetaInfo file and add the old ID to the provides tag.
-      items:
-        - name:
-            If the ID has been renamed, the old ID is present in both a <provides> tag and a <replaces> tag in the MetaInfo
-            file.
-          description: null
-          items: null
-          actions:
-            - SHOW_APP_ID # New app ID
-            - SHOW_OLD_APP_ID # Previous app ID (by looking into git history for submission's repo in flathub GH org)
-            - SHOW_METAINFO_PROVIDES # To check if the old app ID is in provides tag
-            - SHOW_METAINFO_REPLACES # To check if the old app ID is in replaces tag
-        - name:
-            If rename-appdata-file is used in the manifest, the ID tag in the MetaInfo file is updated automatically and the
-            old ID added to <provides>.
-          description: null
-          items: null
