@@ -1,111 +0,0 @@
-<img alt="Project icon" style="vertical-align: middle;" src="./assets/meta/icon.svg" width="128" height="128" align="left">
-
-# Phial
-
-Run development machines safely.
-
-<br/>
-
-[![GNOME Circle](https://circle.gnome.org/assets/button/badge.svg)](https://apps.gnome.org/Phial/)
-[![Please do not theme this app](https://stopthemingmy.app/badge.svg)](https://stopthemingmy.app)
-[![Flatpak CI](https://github.com/pojntfx/phial/actions/workflows/flatpak.yaml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/pojntfx/phial/actions/workflows/flatpak.yaml)
-![Go Version](https://img.shields.io/badge/go%20version-%3E=1.25-61CFDD.svg)
-[![Go Reference](https://pkg.go.dev/badge/github.com/pojntfx/phial.svg)](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/pojntfx/phial)
-[![Matrix](https://img.shields.io/matrix/phial:matrix.org)](https://matrix.to/#/#phial:matrix.org?via=matrix.org)
-[![Weblate translation status](https://hosted.weblate.org/widget/phial/svg-badge.svg)](https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/phial/)
-
-## Overview
-
-Phial is a simple virtual machine manager designed specifically for development work. It keeps every secret and private key on the host while a machine runs.
-
-It enables you to:
-
-- **Create and install development machines** with CPU, memory, disk, and network settings
-- **Grant time-boxed access to tokens and link SSH keys and GnuPG keys** without exposing them to the machine
-- **Review requests from a machine** before you approve them
-- **Pass USB devices, USB hubs, and shared folders** to a machine
-- **Open a remote desktop, a terminal, a serial console, or a guest application**
-
-## Installation
-
-On Linux, Phial is available on Flathub:
-
-<a href='https://flathub.org/apps/com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial'>
-<img width='240' alt='Download on Flathub' src='https://flathub.org/api/badge?locale=en'/>
-</a>
-
-For other platforms, see [contributing](#contributing); development builds are also available on [GitHub releases](https://github.com/pojntfx/phial/releases/tag/release-main).
-
-## Tutorial
-
-Phial runs Fedora virtual machines on your desktop. Every secret and every private key stays on the host. Here is how to use Phial:
-
-1. **Create a machine**: Choose CPU, memory, disk, and network settings
-2. **Install the machine**: Phial runs the installer in seven visible steps
-3. **Start the machine**: Use the power button in the header bar
-4. **Add a token**: Add a token on the Secrets page
-5. **Link a key**: Link an SSH key or a GnuPG key from Passwords and Keys to one machine
-6. **Grant access**: Grant one token to one machine for a set time
-7. **Review requests**: Approve or deny pending requests on the Grants page
-
-Phial does not create, import, or delete SSH keys or GnuPG keys. Manage those keys in Passwords and Keys, then link them to a machine on the Secrets page.
-
-🚀 **You are ready.** We hope Phial helps you keep your secrets safe.
-
-## Screenshots
-
-Select an image to see a larger version.
-
-<a display="inline" href="./assets/meta/screenshot-machine.png?raw=true">
-<img src="./assets/meta/screenshot-machine.png" width="45%" alt="Managing a development machine" title="Managing a development machine">
-</a>
-
-<a display="inline" href="./assets/meta/screenshot-secrets.png?raw=true">
-<img src="./assets/meta/screenshot-secrets.png" width="45%" alt="Tokens and keys" title="Tokens and keys">
-</a>
-
-## Acknowledgements
-
-- [Felicitas Pojtinger](https://felicitas.pojtinger.com/) contributed the icon.
-- [puregotk/puregotk](https://codeberg.org/puregotk/puregotk) provides the GTK4 and `libadwaita` bindings for Go.
-
-## Contributing
-
-If you are new to contributing to open-source projects or projects in the GNOME ecosystem, the [contribution guide](https://welcome.gnome.org/app/Phial/) for Phial can help you.
-
-To contribute, use the [GitHub flow](https://guides.github.com/introduction/flow/) and follow the [GNOME Code of Conduct](https://conduct.gnome.org/).
-
-To build and start a development version of Phial locally, run the following:
-
-```shell
-$ git clone https://github.com/pojntfx/phial.git
-$ cd phial
-$ go generate ./...
-$ go run -ldflags="-X 'main.LocaleDir=${PWD}/po' -X 'main.SchemaDir=${PWD}/assets/resources'" .
-```
-
-You can also open the project in [GNOME Builder](https://flathub.org/apps/org.gnome.Builder) and run it with the play button in the header bar, or use [Foundry](https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/foundry) directly:
-
-```shell
-$ foundry init
-$ foundry run
-```
-
-If you want to reproduce the build from Flathub, you can use [flatpak-builder](https://docs.flathub.org/docs/for-app-authors/submission#before-submission) directly:
-
-```shell
-$ flatpak run --command=flathub-build org.flatpak.Builder --install com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json
-$ flatpak run --command=flatpak-builder-lint org.flatpak.Builder manifest com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial.json
-$ flatpak run --command=flatpak-builder-lint org.flatpak.Builder repo repo
-$ flatpak run com.pojtinger.felicitas.Phial
-```
-
-To translate Phial, you can use [Weblate](https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/phial/). This is the current translation status:
-
-[![Weblate translation status graphs](https://hosted.weblate.org/widget/phial/multi-auto.svg)](https://hosted.weblate.org/engage/phial/)
-
